arately.\n\n- Consider the upper plane ${S}_{1}.$\n\nWe compute the partial derivatives of $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(y-x)=-1 \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(y-x)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we denote $F=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩,$ then\n\n$$\nP=0,\\,Q=y,\\,R=-x.\n$$\n\n \n\nAs a result, since the positive orientation is upward, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{S}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-0\\cdot (-1)-y\\cdot 1+(-x))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-y-x)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Consider lower cone ${S}_{2}.$ \n\nWe compute the partial derivatives of $z=h(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}-9)=\\frac{3x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}} \\\\ \\frac{∂h}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}-9)=\\frac{3y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we denote $F=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩,$ then\n\n$$\nP=0,\\,Q=y,\\,R=-x.\n$$\n\n \n\nAs a result, since the positive orientation is upward, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{S}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & =-{∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-{∬}_{D}(-0\\cdot \\frac{3x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}-y\\cdot \\frac{3y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}+(-x))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-{∬}_{D}(-\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}-x)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}+x)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the flux across the entire surface is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{{S}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S+{∬}_{{S}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-y-x)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{D}(\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}+x)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{3{y}^{2}}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}-y\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139545755 17592186576411 false] [17592186401309 1074 "Since we have a closed surface, the positive orientation is outward-pointing by convention. So,\n\n-